mber","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T21:46:48-07:00","id":1553890,"title":"","content":"Would anyone be brave enough to ask Cain about his lineage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T22:50:33-07:00","id":1553893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1553890#post1553890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone be brave enough to ask Cain about his lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we belive what is written in the Book of Nod (eg. &quot;By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot;) then Caine was a Baali with his own Embrace rite, like the Organ Pit just milder - in that case the whole Cainite race is just one big Infernal Family and/or every clan is just offshots, bloodlines of the Baali and when Saulot pulled his Way of Ten Thousand Screams (or The Howl of the Devil Tiger, dealers choice) stunt with the little village and Children worshippers they just &quot;rediscovered&quot; their heritage in a form of spiritual atavism - it would actually explain why the Baali's level 7 <b>Daimonion </b>power, <b>The Re-Embrace </b><i>works. </i>It resets the cainite to its &quot;(should be) spiritual factory setting&quot; <br /> Or he was Proto-Baali, an Infernalist Caitiff<br /> Of course if he was a vampire <i>at all</i> - I'm pretty sure one of the the requirement to be a vampire is to be dead first, to rise as an undead<br /> Caine never died<br /> But the Second and maybe Third Generation - depends how harshly you define &quot;Clan&quot; were definitely Caitiff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 09-18-2025, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T07:42:31-07:00","id":1553898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1553890#post1553890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would anyone be brave enough to ask Cain about his lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you even believe anyone claiming to be Caine?<br /> <br /> Anything above the Fourth Generation is just theoretical, even the Antes themselves, the concept of clan doesn't even apply to those beings. So whatever they say, you would have only their word for it. At most you would be able to, <i>maybe</i>, verify with <b>Auspex</b> if they believe whatever they're saying.<br /> <br /> The only exception to this would be <b>if</b> everything we &quot;know&quot; is wrong and their lineage can be identified with a Thaumaturgy effect to identify clan, finding out they belong to one of the established clans or lineages. If you use this effect and identify them as either <b>Caitiff</b> or an unknown bloodline, then it means nothing at all, but the Book of Nod may be right after all. It's still possible that the Book of Nod is right if you identify them as Baali, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> said, or some other Bloodline you can theorize as being a proto-clan or non-lineage in the same way.<br /> <br /> But if you find any of those being to belong to a known clan or lineage, even a member of the Third Generation, that's a very weird find. If you're certain they are the Generation in question, or Caine, that means something is off with the Book of Nod, and maybe the whole story isn't quite as true as we think.<br /> <br /> Of course, at first it may seem that a 3rd Gen showing up as a member of the clan they spawned isn't so strange... but they're not actually from those clans. They're childer of the 2nd Generation and very different beings from later vampires, with powers and weaknesses that were, by then, unique to them. They are the cause of the clans, not their effect. Under the premise that the Book of Nod is mostly correct, I would expect them to ping as <b>Caitiff</b> or <b>Unknown</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T10:24:57-07:00","id":1553902,"title":"","content":"No I would be skeptical about a kindred claiming to be Caine let alone one of his childer or grandchilder.<br /> <br /> It's also a given that it's members of the 4th generation that are progenitors of the clans if we go by the Book of Nod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-18-2025, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T22:53:18-07:00","id":1553914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1553902#post1553902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I would be skeptical about a kindred claiming to be Caine let alone one of his childer or grandchilder..</div> </div> </div> </div>Here comes the tricky part<br /> This already happened once in Berlin with <b>Ankla Hotep</b><br /> For their past history, while Ankla laid in torpor, Nefertiti manipulated his mind to forget who he really was and to believe he was Caine.<br /> He was already a powerhouse in his own right, a 5th Generation Ravnos was already a force to be reconed with but Nefertiti upped the ante a bit and gave him an amulet crafted for him by a Bane Mummy - thanks to that his Chimerstry powers increase to the level of an Antediluvian.<br /> While using his Chimerstry, he was<i> for all intents and purposes Caine </i>and could <i>alter reality</i> around him within a five-mile radius.<br /> So he wasn't Caine per see... untill he was<br /> Then he wasn't<br /> It was a trick, sure, but a firghtening one, if you think about it<br /> Bane Mummies are powerfull, yes, but they are not the upper echelon of Apep's servant yet one was managed to create an Amulet that boosted a Ravnos Methuselah not even four millenia old (he was Embraced in Egypt in 1727 BC ) to be the Dark Father himself in a small reality bubble<br /> It is a bit of a &quot;If you meet the Buddha on the road, kill him&quot; situation, except these Buddhas potentially could be right, just from a certain point of view\u200b<br /> If he talks like a dog, barks like a dog, looks like a dog... well... especially if he could back it up with his powers?<br /> <br /> Luckily Vampires are paranoid and untrustworthy bunch with a healthy dose of scepticism even when nailed to the rooftop waiting the Sun to rise <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T23:32:36-07:00","id":1553915,"title":"","content":"I remember that somewhat Shadeprowler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T01:06:37-07:00","id":1553916,"title":"","content":"The smell, they smell pretty bad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-19T01:07:21-07:00","id":1553917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1553914#post1553914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here comes the tricky part<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even think such a display of power is relevant to this.<br /> <br /> Most cities don't even have an 8th Generation vampire, and have only a few Elders with a couple centuries under their belt. For those undead a 5th Gen Methuselah is effectively indistinguishable from an Antediluvian under most circumstances.<br /> <br /> We as players pay a lot of attention to the dice pools and power levels a character can pull off, and as readers we can look at their actual sheets. But characters aren't readers. They can't access what someone is capable of doing, and most of the time have no reason to use their full power openly.<br /> <br /> A guy claiming to be Caine only has to be 1 or 2 Generations lower than the most powerful Kindred around to be virtually impossible to verify without magic. Add to that that powerful vampires don't even necessarily have to use their powers at all. After all, as far as anyone knows the cab driver from <i>Bloodlines</i> could have been Caine himself. A guy claiming to be Caine only has to withstand any attack and cover obvious telltales of clan and done, you can't easily prove he isn't.<br /> <br /> Likewise, what &quot;being Caine in such context&quot; even means? We don't really know what Caine looks like or what powers and weaknesses he has. We have vague ideas, but that's that. How can you point to anyone with greater, stranger powers and say this is or isn't what Caine's powers look like? Someone comes and exhibits powers beyond what any Kindred can do and... so what? What does it really means? It can be anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T17:32:06-07:00","id":1553997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1553774#post1553774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex should help; say, wasn't Cain a Caitiff?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the kind of statement that starts fights in the Sabbat. Heck, that's a statement that's liable to start a whole Crusade.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's arguably true, but some people are going to be really bothered by the implication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T23:07:07-07:00","id":1554001,"title":"","content":"In our game we thought having a 9th generation anciliea was pushing it let alone a 8th generation elder. Our city is barely 150 years old and we thought long and hard on what they most likely ages the major players would be and felt 11th generation kindred with slightly over 150 years could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T07:23:42-07:00","id":1554009,"title":"","content":"Server won't let me quote other people, for reasons, so here we go:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here comes the tricky part<br /> This already happened once in Berlin with <b>Ankla Hotep</b><br /> For their past history, while Ankla laid in torpor, Nefertiti manipulated his mind to forget who he really was and to believe he was Caine.<br /> He was already a powerhouse in his own right, a 5th Generation Ravnos was already a force to be reconed with but Nefertiti upped the ante a bit and gave him an amulet crafted for him by a Bane Mummy - thanks to that his Chimerstry powers increase to the level of an Antediluvian.<br /> While using his Chimerstry, he was<i> for all intents and purposes Caine </i>and could <i>alter reality</i> around him within a five-mile radius.<br /> So he wasn't Caine per see... untill he was<br /> Then he wasn't<br /> It was a trick, sure, but a firghtening one, if you think about it </div> </div> </div>I remember the &quot;Ascension of Caine&quot;\u200b - that adventure is <i><b>very</b> </i>hit-&amp;-miss in many, many aspects, but it did inspire me more than once in tackling the subject of myth x truth and how does kindred society or individuals deal with something rocking the boat and perspectives on legend, truth, fate, status quo and how different groups might converge, react or clash around a newly shown superpower, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't even think such a display of power is relevant to this.\u200b<br /> <br /> Most cities don't even have an 8th Generation vampire, and have only a few Elders with a couple centuries under their belt. For those undead a 5th Gen Methuselah is effectively indistinguishable from an Antediluvian under most circumstances.<br /> <br /> We as players pay a lot of attention to the dice pools and power levels a character can pull off, and as readers we can look at their actual sheets. But characters aren't readers. They can't access what someone is capable of doing, and most of the time have no reason to use their full power openly.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> &quot;<i>Any sufficiently potent individual or display of power of the blood is indistinguishable from legend</i>&quot;, to liberally paraphrase a certain oft-quoted adage.<br /> <br /> Yeah, i agree with you that the immense majority of kindred would have little to no conception of how to separate monsters with powers in the 6+ range from whatever those claim to be unless they are close to or have had previous exposure to someone in roughly the same tier or higher. Auspex or Blood magic aren't all that reliable either, since there's no guarantee a mystery kindred could not have Obfuscate+Auspex or Blood magic to block or subvert any such attempts.<br /> <br /> In my own most recent chronicle this gets kind of turned on its head too - &quot;<i>Ok, you say that guy who claimed to be Caine is not true - but how would you know in the first place? I was there back then, know some tricks you definitely don't and sure as hell found no counterproof. At this point your skepticism and my acceptance are equally immaterial. And yet...he's open, incredibly powerful, knowledgeable, not visibly interested in commanding other kindred and has no qualms about sharing tidbits of occult lore and more with those willing </i>\u200bto listen or debate with him<i>. At that point, does true or false</i>\u200b<i> matter all that much in comparison to how many elders or older beings just hoard secrets like OCD meth addict dragons?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> And that's kind of the whole point of the &quot;Witnesses of Caine&quot; as a sort of iconoclastic answer to noddists and Gehenna Cults with their self-serving elder bias in agendas.<br /> <br /> Though to be fair, the fact the &quot;Witnesses&quot; - or Pilgrims as they are also known due to a sub-faction dedicated to keeping track of Caine's sightings, rumors started by those and visiting them - exist as a &quot;NOTgehenna cult&quot; at least part of the coterie has full membership into and is willing to back them up with info, contacts &amp; so on as they globetrot and react to all kinds of nonsense plays far more of a role in the chronicle than Caine per se as either night messiah, taxi driver or anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-25-2025, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T12:23:03-07:00","id":1554014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1554009#post1554009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though to be fair, the fact the &quot;Witnesses&quot; - or Pilgrims as they are also known due to a sub-faction dedicated to keeping track of Caine's sightings, rumors started by those and visiting them - exist as a &quot;NOTgehenna cult&quot; at least part of the coterie has full membership into and is willing to back them up with info, contacts &amp; so on as they globetrot and react to all kinds of nonsense plays far more of a role in the chronicle than Caine per se as either night messiah, taxi driver or anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>A thing most people regularly forget, sometimes even seasoned STs/DMs, is that legends and gods in stories don't really matter because of what they are as characters, but because of what other characters do because of them. Once the Legend enters the scene they're a character like any other, and as Ur-Shulgi shows they can be quite underwhelming despite immense powers. But other people in the setting do stuff because of their stories, regardless if those stories are true or not, and this stuff is what really makes for awesome games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T15:18:31-07:00","id":1554016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552894-how-does-one-recognize-a-caitiff?p=1554014#post1554014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A thing most people regularly forget, sometimes even seasoned STs/DMs, is that legends and gods in stories don't really matter because of what they are as characters, but because of what other characters do because of them. Once the Legend enters the scene they're a character like any other, and as Ur-Shulgi shows they can be quite underwhelming despite immense powers. But other people in the setting do stuff because of their stories, regardless if those stories are true or not, and this stuff is what really makes for awesome games.</div> </div> </div> </div>So very true. Caine/Kapaneus/Anklahotep has been more of macguffin and excuse to weave some weirdness related to the PCs - such as one of them being Erik, a Gangrel turned in Gargoyle in the events of Vampire: Redemption and &quot;fixed&quot; back to what he was in a fateful encounter with the ancient in LA. I could have left just at that, but the guy got really fervorous about the whole &quot;I was lost but Caine brought me back&quot;, what together with being basically a DA character suddenly finding himself in the 2010s, has made his adaptation process to the contemporary society rocky and quite entertaining.<br /> <br /> (Plus, the cabbie also left him a little cool but kind of loaded souvenir.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T11:10:01-07:00","id":1554106,"title":"","content":"Let's never mention Ur-Shurgi in these hallowed halls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-02T19:38:34-07:00","id":1554118,"title":"","content":"Have any of you played or created Caitiff non player characters for your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}